  "qualifications": [
    "An encoding the flavor cannot encode, RGBA8 and an unknown value return RV_ERR_UNSUPPORTED; Chromium falls back to PNG (red-chromium.json toDataURL.unknownFallsBackToPng, toBlobUnknown).",
    "WEBP depends on the flavor encoder: the probe asserts a RIFF/WEBP image or RV_ERR_UNSUPPORTED from the encoder status; the \"image-encoding-*\" platform facilities report unknown on this runtime (finding for R12 integration).",
    "toBlob completes during rv_canvas_to_blob: there is no callback, and a zero-size canvas gives a NULL Blob as the browser callback gets null.",
    "createImageBitmap sources: <img>, SVG <image>, <canvas>, ImageBitmap, ImageData and Blob. HTMLVideoElement, OffscreenCanvas and VideoFrame are outside slim (ENABLE_VIDEO, ENABLE_OFFSCREEN_CANVAS, ENABLE_WEB_CODECS OFF); CSSStyleImageValue is not a source kind.",
    "ImageBitmap transfer is transferFromImageBitmap, which detaches the source; postMessage transfer needs a script realm.",
    "ImageBitmap buffers are unaccelerated where canvases are (patch 0050); GPU work is paused.",
    "ImageBitmapRenderingContext.canvas is not generated: its single-arm union typedef ImageBitmapCanvas would name a second HTMLCanvasElement type in the F# model (generator defect, queued by root: a single-arm union generates a duplicate F# type for its arm); the app holds the canvas it passed to rv_canvas_get_bitmap_context."
  ],
